{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}
- NestJS 12 REST API in TypeScript, using ES modules
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nextjs')}}
- Next.js 16 with the App Router, React 19, Tailwind CSS 4, and shadcn/ui
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'tanstack')}}
- TanStack Start with Vite, Nitro, React 19, Tailwind CSS 4, and shadcn/ui
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}
- PostgreSQL through Prisma 7
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'drizzle')}}
- PostgreSQL through Drizzle ORM
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'mongoose')}}
- MongoDB through Mongoose
{{/if}}
{{#if useAuth}}
{{#if (eq framework 'express')}}
- JWT auth: `POST /auth/register`, `POST /auth/login`, and `GET /auth/me`
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}
- JWT auth: `POST /auth/register`, `POST /auth/login`, and `GET /auth/me`
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nextjs')}}
- Better Auth with email and password
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'tanstack')}}
- Better Auth with email and password
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if useRateLimit}}
- Rate limiting on every route except `/health`
{{/if}}
{{#if useDocker}}
- Docker: `Dockerfile` and `docker-compose.yml`
{{/if}}
{{#if useCi}}
- GitHub Actions CI in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
{{/if}}
- Package manager: {{packageManager}}. Do not use another one or add its lockfile
- Node.js 24 or later

## Commands

- Install: `{{packageManager}} install`
- Dev server: `{{docker.run}} dev`
- Build: `{{docker.run}} build`
- Type-check: `{{docker.run}} type:check`
- Lint: `{{docker.run}} lint`
{{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}
- After changing `prisma/schema.prisma`: `{{docker.run}} prisma:migrate` creates and applies a migration and regenerates the client
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'drizzle')}}
- After changing the schema: `{{docker.run}} db:generate` writes a migration, then `{{docker.run}} db:migrate` applies it
{{/if}}

## Before you finish

Run type-check and lint, and fix every error they report. Run the build too when you changed config, dependencies, or anything the build reads. Do not report a task as done while any of them fails.

## Layout

{{#if (eq framework 'express')}}
- `src/index.ts`: creates the app, adds middleware, and mounts the routers
- `src/env.ts`: checks the environment variables with Zod at startup, so a missing one stops the server with a clear message
- `src/routes/`: one router per resource, mounted in `src/index.ts`
{{#if useAuth}}
- `src/controllers/`, `src/services/`: request handlers and data access for auth
- `src/middleware/requireAuth.ts`: add it to a route to require a valid JWT
{{/if}}
{{#if useRateLimit}}
- `src/middleware/rateLimit.ts`: the rate limiters
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}
- `src/lib/prisma.ts`: the shared Prisma client. Do not create another one
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'drizzle')}}
- `src/lib/db.ts`, `src/lib/schema.ts`: the database client and the tables
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'mongoose')}}
- `src/lib/db.ts`, `src/models/`: the connection and the Mongoose models
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}
- `src/main.ts`: starts the app
- `src/app.module.ts`: the root module. Register new modules and controllers here
- `src/env.ts`: checks the environment variables with Zod at startup, so a missing one stops the server with a clear message
- `src/health/`: `GET /health`
{{#if useAuth}}
- `src/auth/`: the auth module. Put `@UseGuards(AuthGuard)` on a route to require a valid JWT
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}
- `src/prisma/`: `PrismaService`, injected wherever the database is needed
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'drizzle')}}
- `src/database/`: the database module and the tables in `schema.ts`
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'mongoose')}}
- `src/users/user.schema.ts`: the Mongoose schema for users
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nextjs')}}
- `app/`: routes, layouts, and route handlers. Pages are Server Components unless they need state, effects, or event handlers
- `components/ui/`: shadcn/ui components. Add new ones with the shadcn CLI instead of writing them by hand
- `lib/utils.ts`: the `cn()` class name helper
{{#if useAuth}}
- `lib/auth.ts`: the Better Auth server. `lib/auth-client.ts`: the client for components
- `app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts`: the Better Auth endpoints. Do not rename it
- `proxy.ts`: sends signed-out visitors from `/dashboard` to `/sign-in`. Add other protected paths to its `matcher`
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}
- `lib/prisma.ts`: the shared Prisma client. Do not create another one
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'drizzle')}}
- `lib/db.ts`, `lib/schema.ts`: the database client and the tables
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'mongoose')}}
- `lib/db.ts`, `models/`: the connection and the Mongoose models
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'tanstack')}}
- `src/routes/`: file-based routes. A new file becomes a route
- `src/routeTree.gen.ts`: generated by the dev server and the build. Never edit it
- `src/router.tsx`, `src/routes/__root.tsx`: the router and the root layout
- `src/components/ui/`: shadcn/ui components. Add new ones with the shadcn CLI instead of writing them by hand
- `src/lib/utils.ts`: the `cn()` class name helper
{{#if useAuth}}
- `src/lib/auth.ts`: the Better Auth server. `src/lib/auth-client.ts`: the client for components
- `src/routes/api/auth/$.ts`: the Better Auth endpoints. Do not rename it
- `src/routes/dashboard.tsx`: an example of a protected route that redirects in `beforeLoad`
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}
- `src/lib/prisma.ts`: the shared Prisma client. Do not create another one
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'drizzle')}}
- `src/lib/db.ts`, `src/lib/schema.ts`: the database client and the tables
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'mongoose')}}
- `src/lib/db.ts`, `src/models/`: the connection and the Mongoose models
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

## Rules

- TypeScript is strict. Do not use `any` or `@ts-ignore` to silence an error; fix the type
{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}
- Relative imports end in `.js`, as ES modules require: `import { AuthModule } from "./auth/auth.module.js"`
{{/if}}
- Keep `.env` out of git. When you add an environment variable, add it to `.env.example` too{{#if (eq framework 'express')}}, and to `src/env.ts`{{/if}}{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}, and to `src/env.ts`{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}
- The Prisma client is generated into {{#if (eq framework 'express')}}`src/generated/`{{/if}}{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}`src/generated/`{{/if}}{{#if (eq framework 'nextjs')}}`generated/`{{/if}}{{#if (eq framework 'tanstack')}}`generated/`{{/if}}. Never edit or commit it
{{/if}}
- Match the existing code style. ESLint settings are in `eslint.config.mjs`{{#if (eq framework 'express')}} and Prettier settings in `.prettierrc`{{/if}}{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}} and Prettier settings in `.prettierrc`{{/if}}
- Add a dependency only when the task needs it, and install it with {{packageManager}}

## Production rules

- Validate every input from outside the app (request bodies, query strings, form data) with Zod before you use it{{#unless useAuth}}{{#if (eq framework 'nextjs')}} (add `zod` with {{packageManager}} first){{/if}}{{#if (eq framework 'tanstack')}} (add `zod` with {{packageManager}} first){{/if}}{{/unless}}
- Never log or return secrets, tokens, or passwords. Error responses get a short message and the right status code, never a stack trace
{{#unless (eq database 'none')}}
- Query the database through {{#if (eq database 'prisma')}}Prisma{{/if}}{{#if (eq database 'drizzle')}}Drizzle{{/if}}{{#if (eq database 'mongoose')}}Mongoose{{/if}}, never with SQL or queries built from strings
{{/unless}}
{{#if (eq framework 'express')}}
- Keep the security middleware in `src/index.ts` (`helmet`, `cors`{{#if useRateLimit}}, the rate limiter{{/if}}) in place. Set `CORS_ORIGIN` to your real origins in production
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}
- Keep the security setup in `src/main.ts` and `src/app.module.ts` in place. Set `CORS_ORIGIN` to your real origins in production
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nextjs')}}
- Code that reads secrets or the database stays on the server. Only variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` reach the browser, so never put a secret in one
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'tanstack')}}
- Code that reads secrets or the database runs in server functions or server routes. Only variables prefixed with `VITE_` reach the browser, so never put a secret in one
{{/if}}
{{#if useAuth}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nextjs')}}
- Check the session on the server in every protected page, route handler, and server action. Hiding a button in the UI does not protect anything
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'tanstack')}}
- Check the session on the server in every protected route and server function. Hiding a button in the UI does not protect anything
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'express')}}
- Keep `GET /health` fast and free of auth{{#if useRateLimit}} and rate limiting{{/if}}, so hosts can check that the app is up
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq framework 'nestjs')}}
- Keep `GET /health` fast and free of auth{{#if useRateLimit}} and rate limiting{{/if}}, so hosts can check that the app is up
{{/if}}
- Keep changes small and focused on the task. Do not add layers, abstractions, or files the task does not need

